Subject: [DRAFT] Pong scanout: the v2 layout assertions, switched off

Draft only. Not in any series, nothing here is live, and this patch does not
compile as written -- deliberately.

**While the switch is 0 these assertions do not hold, and that is the design,
not a defect.** Until display signs the v2 semantics there is no v2 layout for
them to describe, so they describe nothing and must not claim otherwise. The
day the switch flips they become the judgement (P-290's shape: an assertion
that never runs is not a criterion).

flip condition: display signs dbuf semantics (token@44 / evict@48 / target@52)
AND pong-scanout-v2-layout-asserts.patch is in series
flip owner: gpu-agent (GPU line)

The flip belongs to that owner's proposal branch. It is not folded into v3 or
into any later revision of the wire proposal, and no other lane turns it on.

Enable it with PONG_SCANOUT_V2_LAYOUT=1 at the moment that condition holds. It
asserts the four numbers the decision fixes: frame size 56, token at 44 where
reserved used to be, evict at 48, target at 52.

Apply after pong-scanout-assert-offsets.patch: that one brings <stddef.h>, and
without it offsetof is not even declared.

--- a/drivers/PongAdreno/PongScanoutWire.h
+++ b/drivers/PongAdreno/PongScanoutWire.h
@@ -34,3 +34,15 @@
 static_assert(PongScanoutMode==0x7000 && PongScanoutWait==0x7002 &&
     PongScanoutComplete==0x7003 && PongScanoutMemory==0x5343 && PongScanoutVersion==1 &&
     PongScanoutBgra==1,"Pong scanout method codes");
+/* The v2 frame layout, dormant until the wire decision lands. Flipping
+ * PONG_SCANOUT_V2_LAYOUT to 1 is the moment these four numbers become the
+ * contract; until then they are a claim about fields that do not exist, and a
+ * claim about a field that is not there is a false fact, so this block stays
+ * switched off. See docs/research/gpu/GPU-27-SCANOUT-WIRE-PROPOSAL.md. */
+#define PONG_SCANOUT_V2_LAYOUT 0
+#if PONG_SCANOUT_V2_LAYOUT
+static_assert(sizeof(PongScanoutFrame)==56,"v2 frame");
+static_assert(offsetof(PongScanoutFrame,token)==44,"v2 token sits where reserved was");
+static_assert(offsetof(PongScanoutFrame,evict)==48,"v2 evict");
+static_assert(offsetof(PongScanoutFrame,target)==52,"v2 target");
+#endif
--- a/drivers/PongMetal/PongMetalScanout.h
+++ b/drivers/PongMetal/PongMetalScanout.h
@@ -250,3 +250,10 @@
     report(result?"scanout worker creation failed":"real GPU scanout worker ready",result);
 }
 }
+/* The same four numbers, asserted where the reader lives, so a reporter names
+ * this file rather than the kernel header. Enable together with the kernel-side
+ * switch; see docs/research/gpu/GPU-27-SCANOUT-WIRE-PROPOSAL.md. */
+#if PONG_SCANOUT_V2_LAYOUT
+static_assert(sizeof(PongScanoutFrame)==56,"presenter: v2 reply is 56 bytes");
+static_assert(offsetof(PongScanoutFrame,target)==52,"presenter: v2 target offset");
+#endif
